  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Doctrine and Covenants",
    "delineation": "Section",
    "number": 27,
    "summary": "1–4, The emblems to be used in partaking of the sacrament are set forth; 5–14, Christ and His servants from all dispensations are to partake of the sacrament; 15–18, Put on the whole armor of God.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [
      {
        "type": "introduction",
        "text": "Revelation given to Joseph Smith the Prophet, at Harmony, Pennsylvania, August 1830. In preparation for a religious service at which the sacrament of bread and wine was to be administered, Joseph set out to procure wine. He was met by a heavenly messenger and received this revelation, a portion of which was written at the time and the remainder in the September following. Water is now used instead of wine in the sacramental services of the Church."
      }
    ],
